    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95-a1">

                <pb facs="0274" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg216"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 1.</seg></opener>
                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 271.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of Foreign Relations and
                                Government</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 18, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I send you for your information copies of the circular I have addressed to the
                    State governors, informing them that the President arrived in this city
                    yesterday, where he returns to fix the seat of the national government for the
                    time being.</p>
                <p>I protest to you my attentive consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LERDO DE TEJADA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Citizen <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matias Romero, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Envoy Extraordinary and Minister of the Mexican Republic in
                                Washington</hi></hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
